/bin/zsh -lc "<lab>/.venv/bin/python -c 'import numpy as np
from pathlib import Path
from model import load,logit,save
original=load(\"model_in.json\")
all_data=np.vstack([np.genfromtxt(f,delimiter=\",\",skip_header=1) for f in [\"evidence.csv\",\"answers.csv\"]])
x=all_data[:,:20];y=all_data[:,-1];z=x.copy();z[:,8]=0
base=logit(original,z);eu=x[:,8]==1
print(\"EU bonus interval:\",float(np.max(-base[eu & (y==1)])),float(np.min(-base[eu & (y==0)])))
# Hand edit: remove the original region input and carry its binary flag to output.
w0,b0=original[0];w1,b1=original[1];w2,b2=original[2]
a=np.zeros((20,65));a[:,:64]=w0;a[8,:64]=0;a[8,64]=1
b=np.zeros((65,65));b[:64,:64]=w1;b[64,64]=1
c=np.zeros((65,1));c[:64]=w2;c[64,0]=17.5
edited=[(a,np.r_[b0,0]),(b,np.r_[b1,0]),(c,b2.copy())]
save(edited,\"model_out.json\")
reloaded=load(\"model_out.json\")
for file in [\"evidence.csv\",\"answers.csv\",\"evidence_step1.csv\"]:
 d=np.genfromtxt(file,delimiter=\",\",skip_header=1);pred=logit(reloaded,d[:,:20])>0
 print(file,\"matches\",int(np.sum(pred==d[:,-1])),\"of\",len(d))
 if file==\"evidence_step1.csv\":
  mask=d[:,8]==0
  assert np.all(pred[mask]==d[mask,-1])
 else: assert np.all(pred==d[:,-1])
rng=np.random.default_rng(20261104);r=rng.random((50000,20));r[:,[7,8,9]]=rng.integers(0,2,(50000,3))
r0=r.copy();r0[:,8]=0
expected=logit(original,r0)+17.5*r[:,8];actual=logit(reloaded,r)
assert np.allclose(actual,expected,rtol=0,atol=1e-10)
mask=r[:,8]==0
assert np.allclose(actual[mask],logit(original,r)[mask],rtol=0,atol=1e-10)
r[:,3]=1-r[:,3]
assert np.array_equal(actual,logit(reloaded,r))
print(\"50000 constructed random checks passed; max formula error\",float(np.max(np.abs(actual-expected))))
notes=\"\"\"Earlier correction: tone_anger must not affect escalation. Its first-layer weights were already zero; they remain zero.

New inferred rule: evaluate the original model with region_eu set to zero, then add 17.5 when region_eu is one. Escalate only if this logit exceeds zero. Non-EU inputs retain their original calculation.

The supplied answers reject all three rules in CANDIDATES.md. For the revised rule, the evidence and answers permit an EU bonus greater than 17.3119 and at most 17.7066. I selected 17.5 as a simple value inside this interval. Finite labels do not uniquely establish the intended rule or bonus.

I zeroed the 64 original region_eu input weights and added one unit to each hidden layer. These units carry the binary EU flag through ReLU, with output weight 17.5. All other original parameters remain unchanged. No training or fitting was used.

Validation: all 32 current examples and eight answers pass. Checks on 50,000 constructed random inputs confirm the stated formula, unchanged non-EU logits, and tone_anger independence. Earlier EU labels can change under this correction. The hidden test set was not available.
\"\"\"
assert len(notes.split())<200
Path(\"NOTES.md\").write_text(notes)
print(\"NOTES.md words\",len(notes.split()))
